OL,3,GNEWSASergeant who showed colleagues
OL,4,A'offensive' meme sacked
OL,5,
OL,6,FA police sergeant who showed colleagues
OL,7,Fan "offensive" meme referring to a
OL,8,F"date rape" drug while working as a
OL,9,Fsupervisor has been dismissed without
OL,10,Fnotice.
OL,12,FDavid Brenchley, who worked for Thames
OL,13,FValley Police, was also alleged to have
OL,14,Ftouched a female officer in an
OL,15,F"inappropriate and overly familiar" way
OL,16,Fin 2021 and to have made "inappropriate
OL,17,Fand unprofessional comments" on a
OL,18,Fnumber of occasions in 2025.
OL,20,FThese included sexualised innuendos, as
OL,21,Fwell as homophobic and misogynistic
OL,22,Fcomments.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
